{"_e":"metro:client_log","_t":1786216671035,"level":"log","data":["Response body:","{\"answer_id\":77,\"total_score\":9,\"scores\":{\"situation\":6,\"task\":2,\"action\":1,\"result\":0},\"strengths\":[\"The candidate acknowledges experiencing a negative emotional response.\"],\"improvements\":[\"The answer is extremely brief and lacks context. It doesn't explain the situation that led to the setback.\",\"It fails to demonstrate any proactive problem-solving or learning from the experience.\",\"The response feels overly simplistic and unprofessional for a job interview.\"],\"feedback\":\"This response demonstrates a very limited understanding of how to handle setbacks. While acknowledging emotions is important, this answer needs significant development to showcase resilience, self-awareness, and a commitment to improvement. The candidate needs to articulate the circumstances surrounding the setback and their approach to overcoming it.\",\"suggested_answer\":\"Okay, let me tell you about a time I faced a particularly challenging situation during my recent training for the regional marathon. (Situation) I had been diligently following my training plan, but in the week leading up to the race, I developed a severe case of shin splints – intense pain on the outside of my left leg. This meant I couldn't run at all, and it was incredibly frustrating because I’d invested so much time and effort. (Task) My goal was to still complete the marathon, but I needed to find a way to manage the pain and continue training effectively. (Action) Recognizing that simply pushing through would likely worsen the injury, I immediately consulted with my physical therapist who adjusted my treatment plan, focusing on targeted stretching and ice therapy. I also modified my training schedule, switching to low-impact cross-training like swimming and cycling while carefully monitoring my leg. (Result) While I didn’t achieve my original race time, I was able to finish the marathon, albeit slower than planned, and more importantly, I learned a valuable lesson about listening to my body and prioritizing recovery. This experience ultimately strengthened my understanding of injury prevention and helped me develop a more sustainable training approach.\"}"]}
{"_e":"metro:client_log","_t":1786216671039,"level":"log","data":["STAR evaluation:","{\"answer_id\": 77, \"feedback\": \"This response demonstrates a very limited understanding of how to handle setbacks. While acknowledging emotions is important, this answer needs significant development to showcase resilience, self-awareness, and a commitment to improvement. The candidate needs to articulate the circumstances surrounding the setback and their approach to overcoming it.\", \"improvements\": [\"The answer is extremely brief and lacks context. It doesn't explain the situation that led to the setback.\", \"It fails to demonstrate any proactive problem-solving or learning from the experience.\", \"The response feels overly simplistic and unprofessional for a job interview.\"], \"scores\": {\"action\": 1, \"result\": 0, \"situation\": 6, \"task\": 2}, \"strengths\": [\"The candidate acknowledges experiencing a negative emotional response.\"], \"suggested_answer\": \"Okay, let me tell you about a time I faced a particularly challenging situation during my recent training for the regional marathon. (Situation) I had been diligently following my training plan, but in the week leading up to the race, I developed a severe case of shin splints – intense pain on the outside of my left leg. This meant I couldn't run at all, and it was incredibly frustrating because I’d invested so much time and effort. (Task) My goal was to still complete the marathon, but I needed to find a way to manage the pain and continue training effectively. (Action) Recognizing that simply pushing through would likely worsen the injury, I immediately consulted with my physical therapist who adjusted my treatment plan, focusing on targeted stretching and ice therapy. I also modified my training schedule, switching to low-impact cross-training like swimming and cycling while carefully monitoring my leg. (Result) While I didn’t achieve my original race time, I was able to finish the marathon, albeit slower than planned, and more importantly, I learned a valuable lesson about listening to my body and prioritizing recovery. This experience ultimately strengthened my understanding of injury prevention and helped me develop a more sustainable training approach.\", \"total_score\": 9}"]}
