{"_e":"metro:client_log","_t":1786217376328,"level":"log","data":["Response body:","{\"answer_id\":84,\"total_score\":15,\"scores\":{\"situation\":6,\"task\":3,\"action\":4,\"result\":2},\"strengths\":[\"The candidate clearly identifies a high-pressure situation – Game 7 of the World Series.\"],\"improvements\":[\"The response lacks detail regarding the context surrounding the at-bat. What was the score? What inning was it? What were the team’s strategic goals?\",\"The description of the action is extremely brief and doesn't convey how they maintained focus. It relies on a potentially unprofessional phrase.\",\"There is no mention of the outcome or impact beyond scoring the winning run.\"],\"feedback\":\"This response demonstrates awareness of a critical moment but needs significant development to fully utilize the STAR method. The candidate’s recounting feels rushed and lacks crucial details that would showcase resilience effectively.\",\"suggested_answer\":\"\\\"During Game 7 of the World Series, with two outs in the bottom of the ninth inning and the score tied at three, I was stepping up to bat. My team needed a single to win the championship. I hit a ground ball sharply to shortstop, which unfortunately resulted in an error that allowed me to reach first base. Despite the mistake, I immediately focused on my next objective: advancing to second. I took a deep breath, reminded myself of our game plan, and continued running aggressively. I successfully reached second base, and with a stolen base, I scored the winning run, securing the championship for my team. This experience taught me the importance of quickly recovering from setbacks and maintaining composure under immense pressure.\\\"\"}"]}
{"_e":"metro:client_log","_t":1786217376331,"level":"log","data":["STAR evaluation:","{\"answer_id\": 84, \"feedback\": \"This response demonstrates awareness of a critical moment but needs significant development to fully utilize the STAR method. The candidate’s recounting feels rushed and lacks crucial details that would showcase resilience effectively.\", \"improvements\": [\"The response lacks detail regarding the context surrounding the at-bat. What was the score? What inning was it? What were the team’s strategic goals?\", \"The description of the action is extremely brief and doesn't convey how they maintained focus. It relies on a potentially unprofessional phrase.\", \"There is no mention of the outcome or impact beyond scoring the winning run.\"], \"scores\": {\"action\": 4, \"result\": 2, \"situation\": 6, \"task\": 3}, \"strengths\": [\"The candidate clearly identifies a high-pressure situation – Game 7 of the World Series.\"], \"suggested_answer\": \"\\\"During Game 7 of the World Series, with two outs in the bottom of the ninth inning and the score tied at three, I was stepping up to bat. My team needed a single to win the championship. I hit a ground ball sharply to shortstop, which unfortunately resulted in an error that allowed me to reach first base. Despite the mistake, I immediately focused on my next objective: advancing to second. I took a deep breath, reminded myself of our game plan, and continued running aggressively. I successfully reached second base, and with a stolen base, I scored the winning run, securing the championship for my team. This experience taught me the importance of quickly recovering from setbacks and maintaining composure under immense pressure.\\\"\", \"total_score\": 15}"]}
