{"_e":"metro:client_log","_t":1786217443015,"level":"log","data":["Response body:","{\"answer_id\":85,\"total_score\":7,\"scores\":{\"situation\":6,\"task\":0,\"action\":1,\"result\":0},\"strengths\":[\"The candidate acknowledges receiving criticism.\"],\"improvements\":[\"The response lacks context. It doesn't describe the situation where this occurred.\",\"There is no mention of a coach or teammate, only an 'umpire'.\",\"The description of the action is extremely brief and doesn't demonstrate any reflection or learning.\"],\"feedback\":\"This response demonstrates a reactive rather than reflective approach to constructive criticism. It needs significant development to effectively address this behavioral question.\",\"suggested_answer\":\"Let me tell you about a time I was playing baseball and the umpire wasn't consistently calling balls and strikes correctly. Specifically, he kept missing calls on pitches that were clearly outside the strike zone. This created a frustrating situation for the team as it impacted our strategy. Initially, I felt frustrated because I wanted to ensure fair play and believed the umpire needed to understand the proper definition of the strike zone. I calmly approached him after the inning and politely explained my understanding of the rules, pointing out several specific pitches that were missed. To my surprise, he initially dismissed me, but I persisted in explaining my reasoning clearly and respectfully. Eventually, he acknowledged his oversight and adjusted his calls for the remainder of the game. This experience taught me the importance of calmly advocating for what you believe is right while also recognizing the perspective of others. It reinforced the value of clear communication and respectful disagreement.\"}"]}
{"_e":"metro:client_log","_t":1786217443015,"level":"log","data":["STAR evaluation:","{\"answer_id\": 85, \"feedback\": \"This response demonstrates a reactive rather than reflective approach to constructive criticism. It needs significant development to effectively address this behavioral question.\", \"improvements\": [\"The response lacks context. It doesn't describe the situation where this occurred.\", \"There is no mention of a coach or teammate, only an 'umpire'.\", \"The description of the action is extremely brief and doesn't demonstrate any reflection or learning.\"], \"scores\": {\"action\": 1, \"result\": 0, \"situation\": 6, \"task\": 0}, \"strengths\": [\"The candidate acknowledges receiving criticism.\"], \"suggested_answer\": \"Let me tell you about a time I was playing baseball and the umpire wasn't consistently calling balls and strikes correctly. Specifically, he kept missing calls on pitches that were clearly outside the strike zone. This created a frustrating situation for the team as it impacted our strategy. Initially, I felt frustrated because I wanted to ensure fair play and believed the umpire needed to understand the proper definition of the strike zone. I calmly approached him after the inning and politely explained my understanding of the rules, pointing out several specific pitches that were missed. To my surprise, he initially dismissed me, but I persisted in explaining my reasoning clearly and respectfully. Eventually, he acknowledged his oversight and adjusted his calls for the remainder of the game. This experience taught me the importance of calmly advocating for what you believe is right while also recognizing the perspective of others. It reinforced the value of clear communication and respectful disagreement.\", \"total_score\": 7}"]}
