{"_e":"metro:client_log","_t":1786236803380,"level":"log","data":["Response body:","{\"answer_id\":90,\"total_score\":4,\"scores\":{\"situation\":3,\"task\":1,\"action\":0,\"result\":0},\"strengths\":[\"The candidate acknowledges a relevant topic – identifying opportunities for improvement in ML models or pipelines.\"],\"improvements\":[\"The response is extremely brief and lacks any context. It doesn't provide *any* information about the situation, task, action, or result.\",\"The candidate failed to demonstrate an understanding of how to answer a behavioral question using the STAR method.\"],\"feedback\":\"This response is wholly inadequate for a behavioral interview question. The candidate provided no substance and demonstrated a lack of preparation. A more detailed explanation is absolutely necessary.\",\"suggested_answer\":\"Okay, let me walk you through an example. At my previous role at [Company Name], we were using a model to predict customer churn. Initially, the model had a decent accuracy rate of 75%, but our team was struggling to proactively reach out to customers identified as high-risk. The task for me was to investigate why the model wasn't translating into actionable insights and ultimately improve its performance. I noticed that the features we were using – primarily website activity and purchase history – weren’t consistently updated, leading to stale data. My proposed change was to implement a daily refresh of these features, pulling the most recent information from our CRM system. We also added a new feature reflecting customer support interactions. To measure the impact, I tracked the model's accuracy after implementing the changes and, more importantly, we monitored the number of customers successfully retained through targeted outreach based on the updated predictions. After one month, the model’s accuracy increased to 82%, and we saw a 15% increase in customer retention.\"}"]}
{"_e":"metro:client_log","_t":1786236803380,"level":"log","data":["STAR evaluation:","{\"answer_id\": 90, \"feedback\": \"This response is wholly inadequate for a behavioral interview question. The candidate provided no substance and demonstrated a lack of preparation. A more detailed explanation is absolutely necessary.\", \"improvements\": [\"The response is extremely brief and lacks any context. It doesn't provide *any* information about the situation, task, action, or result.\", \"The candidate failed to demonstrate an understanding of how to answer a behavioral question using the STAR method.\"], \"scores\": {\"action\": 0, \"result\": 0, \"situation\": 3, \"task\": 1}, \"strengths\": [\"The candidate acknowledges a relevant topic – identifying opportunities for improvement in ML models or pipelines.\"], \"suggested_answer\": \"Okay, let me walk you through an example. At my previous role at [Company Name], we were using a model to predict customer churn. Initially, the model had a decent accuracy rate of 75%, but our team was struggling to proactively reach out to customers identified as high-risk. The task for me was to investigate why the model wasn't translating into actionable insights and ultimately improve its performance. I noticed that the features we were using – primarily website activity and purchase history – weren’t consistently updated, leading to stale data. My proposed change was to implement a daily refresh of these features, pulling the most recent information from our CRM system. We also added a new feature reflecting customer support interactions. To measure the impact, I tracked the model's accuracy after implementing the changes and, more importantly, we monitored the number of customers successfully retained through targeted outreach based on the updated predictions. After one month, the model’s accuracy increased to 82%, and we saw a 15% increase in customer retention.\", \"total_score\": 4}"]}
