{"_e":"metro:client_log","_t":1786237606975,"level":"log","data":["Response body:","{\"answer_id\":95,\"total_score\":24,\"scores\":{\"situation\":6,\"task\":6,\"action\":7,\"result\":5},\"strengths\":[\"The candidate acknowledges a situation where an error occurred.\"],\"improvements\":[\"The response is extremely brief and lacks any detail. It needs significant expansion to demonstrate the STAR method effectively. The candidate must provide context about the situation, their responsibility, what they did, and the outcome.  Specifically, describe the nature of the error, its impact, and the steps taken to rectify it.\"],\"feedback\":\"This response is extremely weak due to a complete lack of detail. To improve, you need to flesh out this answer with specifics about the situation, your role, what went wrong, how you addressed it, and what preventative measures you implemented.  Consider adding 2-3 sentences for each element of the STAR method.\",\"suggested_answer\":\"Okay, let me walk you through a time when I made a significant error that impacted a project. (Situation) We were developing a new marketing campaign for our flagship product, and I was responsible for compiling all the finalized creative assets – images, videos, and copy – into a single deliverable package for the design team. I rushed to get everything together before a critical deadline, and in my haste, I accidentally excluded one of the key promotional videos from the final file. (Task) My responsibility was to ensure all materials were properly prepared and delivered on time. The consequence was that the design team didn't have the complete assets, which delayed their ability to begin designing the campaign mockups by two days. (Action) When I realized my mistake, I immediately notified my manager and the lead designer. We worked together to quickly locate the missing video file, which had been inadvertently saved on an old drive. I then meticulously checked all subsequent files to ensure everything was included correctly. To prevent this in the future, I implemented a new checklist process for compiling asset packages – a detailed list of every file type and their associated links that I review with a colleague before sending it out. (Result) As a result of my swift action and the implementation of the checklist, we were able to minimize the delay and get the campaign back on track. The design team was able to start working immediately, and we ultimately launched the campaign successfully, albeit slightly behind schedule. I learned the importance of meticulousness and double-checking my work, especially when under pressure. It reinforced the need for a robust quality control process.\"}"]}
{"_e":"metro:client_log","_t":1786237606975,"level":"log","data":["STAR evaluation:","{\"answer_id\": 95, \"feedback\": \"This response is extremely weak due to a complete lack of detail. To improve, you need to flesh out this answer with specifics about the situation, your role, what went wrong, how you addressed it, and what preventative measures you implemented.  Consider adding 2-3 sentences for each element of the STAR method.\", \"improvements\": [\"The response is extremely brief and lacks any detail. It needs significant expansion to demonstrate the STAR method effectively. The candidate must provide context about the situation, their responsibility, what they did, and the outcome.  Specifically, describe the nature of the error, its impact, and the steps taken to rectify it.\"], \"scores\": {\"action\": 7, \"result\": 5, \"situation\": 6, \"task\": 6}, \"strengths\": [\"The candidate acknowledges a situation where an error occurred.\"], \"suggested_answer\": \"Okay, let me walk you through a time when I made a significant error that impacted a project. (Situation) We were developing a new marketing campaign for our flagship product, and I was responsible for compiling all the finalized creative assets – images, videos, and copy – into a single deliverable package for the design team. I rushed to get everything together before a critical deadline, and in my haste, I accidentally excluded one of the key promotional videos from the final file. (Task) My responsibility was to ensure all materials were properly prepared and delivered on time. The consequence was that the design team didn't have the complete assets, which delayed their ability to begin designing the campaign mockups by two days. (Action) When I realized my mistake, I immediately notified my manager and the lead designer. We worked together to quickly locate the missing video file, which had been inadvertently saved on an old drive. I then meticulously checked all subsequent files to ensure everything was included correctly. To prevent this in the future, I implemented a new checklist process for compiling asset packages – a detailed list of every file type and their associated links that I review with a colleague before sending it out. (Result) As a result of my swift action and the implementation of the checklist, we were able to minimize the delay and get the campaign back on track. The design team was able to start working immediately, and we ultimately launched the campaign successfully, albeit slightly behind schedule. I learned the importance of meticulousness and double-checking my work, especially when under pressure. It reinforced the need for a robust quality control process.\", \"total_score\": 24}"]}
