{"_e":"metro:client_log","_t":1786237988139,"level":"log","data":["Response body:","{\"answer_id\":98,\"total_score\":0,\"scores\":{\"situation\":0,\"task\":0,\"action\":0,\"result\":0},\"strengths\":[\"The candidate attempted to answer the question.\"],\"improvements\":[\"The response is completely inadequate and provides no information about the situation, task, action, or result. It simply states 'I gave an example' which doesn’t demonstrate any understanding of the question or provide a relevant story.\"],\"feedback\":\"This response demonstrates a significant misunderstanding of the interview question and the STAR method. The candidate needs to articulate a specific experience related to improving an ML model or pipeline.\",\"suggested_answer\":\"Okay, let me tell you about a time when I noticed an opportunity to improve our fraud detection model. (Situation) Our team was using a logistic regression model to flag potentially fraudulent transactions. We were seeing a high false positive rate – meaning legitimate customers were being incorrectly flagged as suspicious. (Task) My task was to investigate the root cause of this issue and propose solutions to reduce the false positives while maintaining our fraud detection accuracy. (Action) I started by analyzing the feature importance from the model, which revealed that transaction amount was heavily weighted. I then proposed adding a new feature – ‘transaction frequency over the last 30 days’ – to capture customers who might be engaging in unusual spending patterns. We implemented this feature and retrained the model. (Result) After retraining, we saw a significant decrease in false positives – about a 15% reduction – while maintaining our fraud detection rate at 98%. This resulted in fewer customer service inquiries related to fraudulent charges and improved overall customer satisfaction.\"}"]}
{"_e":"metro:client_log","_t":1786237988140,"level":"log","data":["STAR evaluation:","{\"answer_id\": 98, \"feedback\": \"This response demonstrates a significant misunderstanding of the interview question and the STAR method. The candidate needs to articulate a specific experience related to improving an ML model or pipeline.\", \"improvements\": [\"The response is completely inadequate and provides no information about the situation, task, action, or result. It simply states 'I gave an example' which doesn’t demonstrate any understanding of the question or provide a relevant story.\"], \"scores\": {\"action\": 0, \"result\": 0, \"situation\": 0, \"task\": 0}, \"strengths\": [\"The candidate attempted to answer the question.\"], \"suggested_answer\": \"Okay, let me tell you about a time when I noticed an opportunity to improve our fraud detection model. (Situation) Our team was using a logistic regression model to flag potentially fraudulent transactions. We were seeing a high false positive rate – meaning legitimate customers were being incorrectly flagged as suspicious. (Task) My task was to investigate the root cause of this issue and propose solutions to reduce the false positives while maintaining our fraud detection accuracy. (Action) I started by analyzing the feature importance from the model, which revealed that transaction amount was heavily weighted. I then proposed adding a new feature – ‘transaction frequency over the last 30 days’ – to capture customers who might be engaging in unusual spending patterns. We implemented this feature and retrained the model. (Result) After retraining, we saw a significant decrease in false positives – about a 15% reduction – while maintaining our fraud detection rate at 98%. This resulted in fewer customer service inquiries related to fraudulent charges and improved overall customer satisfaction.\", \"total_score\": 0}"]}
