{"_e":"metro:client_log","_t":1786237998535,"level":"log","data":["Response body:","{\"answer_id\":99,\"total_score\":6,\"scores\":{\"situation\":3,\"task\":1,\"action\":2,\"result\":0},\"strengths\":[\"The candidate acknowledged encountering a challenge.\"],\"improvements\":[\"The response is extremely brief and provides no context. It needs significant elaboration to demonstrate understanding of the problem-solving process.\"],\"feedback\":\"This answer demonstrates a minimal recognition of the question but fails to provide any substantive information about the challenge, diagnostic steps, or resolution. The candidate needs to articulate a real situation.\",\"suggested_answer\":\"\\\"I encountered a significant challenge while developing a customer churn prediction model for a subscription-based service. Initially, the model had very low accuracy – only 60% - which was far below our expectations. The Situation was that we were relying on historical data and hadn’t accounted for recent changes in user behavior due to a new competitor entering the market. My Task was to diagnose why the model wasn't performing well and improve its predictive power. I started by thoroughly examining the feature importance, which revealed that several key features related to engagement had become less relevant. Then, I investigated data quality issues – we discovered some missing values in user activity logs. To address this, I implemented imputation techniques for the missing data. Finally, I added new features reflecting the impact of the competitor’s entry, such as frequency of competitor app usage. This resulted in a significant improvement in model accuracy to 85% and allowed us to proactively identify at-risk customers.\\\"\"}"]}
{"_e":"metro:client_log","_t":1786237998535,"level":"log","data":["STAR evaluation:","{\"answer_id\": 99, \"feedback\": \"This answer demonstrates a minimal recognition of the question but fails to provide any substantive information about the challenge, diagnostic steps, or resolution. The candidate needs to articulate a real situation.\", \"improvements\": [\"The response is extremely brief and provides no context. It needs significant elaboration to demonstrate understanding of the problem-solving process.\"], \"scores\": {\"action\": 2, \"result\": 0, \"situation\": 3, \"task\": 1}, \"strengths\": [\"The candidate acknowledged encountering a challenge.\"], \"suggested_answer\": \"\\\"I encountered a significant challenge while developing a customer churn prediction model for a subscription-based service. Initially, the model had very low accuracy – only 60% - which was far below our expectations. The Situation was that we were relying on historical data and hadn’t accounted for recent changes in user behavior due to a new competitor entering the market. My Task was to diagnose why the model wasn't performing well and improve its predictive power. I started by thoroughly examining the feature importance, which revealed that several key features related to engagement had become less relevant. Then, I investigated data quality issues – we discovered some missing values in user activity logs. To address this, I implemented imputation techniques for the missing data. Finally, I added new features reflecting the impact of the competitor’s entry, such as frequency of competitor app usage. This resulted in a significant improvement in model accuracy to 85% and allowed us to proactively identify at-risk customers.\\\"\", \"total_score\": 6}"]}
