{"_e":"metro:client_log","_t":1786238075827,"level":"log","data":["Response body:","{\"answer_id\":102,\"total_score\":6,\"scores\":{\"situation\":3,\"task\":2,\"action\":1,\"result\":0},\"strengths\":[\"The candidate identified a relevant project area – data cleaning and preprocessing for model training.\"],\"improvements\":[\"The response is extremely vague and lacks crucial context. It doesn't describe the situation, the specific task assigned to the candidate, or any actions taken.\",\"It fails to address collaboration with other engineers, which was a key part of the question.\"],\"feedback\":\"This answer provides almost no useful information. It’s essentially just stating the project's goal without providing any details about how the candidate contributed or navigated challenges within a collaborative environment.\",\"suggested_answer\":\"Okay, let me tell you about a recent project where collaboration was absolutely essential. We were tasked with building a predictive model to forecast customer churn for our subscription service. The data scientists had built an initial model, but the raw data was incredibly messy – filled with missing values and inconsistent formatting. My role was to lead the effort in cleaning and preprocessing this data so it could be fed into the model. I worked closely with two data scientists, Sarah and David, who were responsible for building and training the predictive models. We had daily stand-up meetings where we discussed progress, identified roadblocks, and shared insights. Initially, there was some disagreement about the best approach to handling missing values – Sarah favored imputation techniques while David preferred a more conservative approach of removing rows with missing data. To resolve this, I facilitated a discussion, presenting the potential biases introduced by each method and ultimately we agreed on a hybrid approach that combined imputation with targeted removal based on specific variables. This collaborative process ensured the model was robust and accurate.\"}"]}
{"_e":"metro:client_log","_t":1786238075829,"level":"log","data":["STAR evaluation:","{\"answer_id\": 102, \"feedback\": \"This answer provides almost no useful information. It’s essentially just stating the project's goal without providing any details about how the candidate contributed or navigated challenges within a collaborative environment.\", \"improvements\": [\"The response is extremely vague and lacks crucial context. It doesn't describe the situation, the specific task assigned to the candidate, or any actions taken.\", \"It fails to address collaboration with other engineers, which was a key part of the question.\"], \"scores\": {\"action\": 1, \"result\": 0, \"situation\": 3, \"task\": 2}, \"strengths\": [\"The candidate identified a relevant project area – data cleaning and preprocessing for model training.\"], \"suggested_answer\": \"Okay, let me tell you about a recent project where collaboration was absolutely essential. We were tasked with building a predictive model to forecast customer churn for our subscription service. The data scientists had built an initial model, but the raw data was incredibly messy – filled with missing values and inconsistent formatting. My role was to lead the effort in cleaning and preprocessing this data so it could be fed into the model. I worked closely with two data scientists, Sarah and David, who were responsible for building and training the predictive models. We had daily stand-up meetings where we discussed progress, identified roadblocks, and shared insights. Initially, there was some disagreement about the best approach to handling missing values – Sarah favored imputation techniques while David preferred a more conservative approach of removing rows with missing data. To resolve this, I facilitated a discussion, presenting the potential biases introduced by each method and ultimately we agreed on a hybrid approach that combined imputation with targeted removal based on specific variables. This collaborative process ensured the model was robust and accurate.\", \"total_score\": 6}"]}
